Exception: the Yie Ar Kung-Fu sprite artwork (assets/oolong-sheet.png and the
build/yiear.bin data derived from it) is copyright Konami and is NOT covered
by this licence; it is included for personal and educational use only.

Music: the melody used by the 128K edition is "Korobeiniki", a Russian folk
tune of the 1860s (melody traditional; lyrics after Nikolay Nekrasov, 1861).
The melody is in the public domain and needs no licence. The three-voice
arrangement in tools/gen_ay128.py -- the bass line, the percussion, and the
per-voice volume envelopes -- is original to this project and is covered by
the licence above. This demo is not affiliated with, and does not reference,
any commercial game that has set the same folk melody.

Motion capture: the runner's source joints are CMU Graphics Lab clip 09_01,
converted to BVH by Bruce Hahne. See assets/mocap/SOURCE.md and READMEFIRST.txt
for provenance, unrestricted reuse terms and the requested acknowledgment.
The database was created with funding from NSF EIA-0196217.

The current music also includes the public-domain melody Ode to Joy by
Beethoven and two original melodies, Neon Drive and Night Flight. Their
arrangements and the original melodies are covered by the project licence.

